        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "ci: add process exec CodeQL security shard",
        "body": "## Summary\n- add a `process-exec-boundary` CodeQL high-security shard for local shell, subprocess helpers, subprocess-owning bundled plugin runtimes, and workflow script glue\n- wire the new shard into the existing `CodeQL` security matrix and PR/push path filters\n- document the new security category and expanded trigger scope in CI docs\n\n## Why\n- supersedes #74437, which added a stale manual-only `local-shell` shard\n- current main already covers part of `src/process/**`, but leaves TUI local shell, Plugin SDK/Memory host spawn helpers, key bundled plugin subprocess runtimes, and workflow Node scripts outside the JavaScript/TypeScript security baseline\n- keeps the current high/critical `security-severity` CodeQL filter contract instead of adding a broader manual profile\n\n## Verification\n- `git diff --check`\n- `pnpm docs:list`\n- `node scripts/check-workflows.mjs`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` -> clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n",
